# cube
Spinning ASCII cubes: three cubes rotated in 3D and projected through a z-buffer into a 160 x 44 character
frame (the classic rotating-cube demo). Core-only Spiral: loops, mutable cells, arrays and float math run on every
backend; the only effect is printing. A run renders `frames` frames, each preceded by ESC[H (cursor home, so a
terminal redraws in place), then prints a checksum of all frames.
## cube
